"\\\\n+**Specification:** \u00a79.1 R9.4, Appendices A, E.38; `params/flop-protocol-params.yaml` (`genesis_reserve`).\\\\n+\\\\n+---\\\\n+\\\\n+## D-0532 \u2014 Miner capacity bond: one unit, window inside the coefficient, value set against a security envelope\\\\n+\\\\n+**Status:** proposal pending ratification (#1361). Amends D-0418; does not supersede its curve shape.\\\\n+Nothing changes in the runtime, `params/` or published surfaces until the owner ratifies it and the\\\\n+activation gates below are met.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Context.** #1361 found three miner capacity-stake numbers in circulation. They reduce to one formula\\\\n+and one implementation error (analysis):\\\\n+\\\\n+- D-0418 and \u00a76.1 require `10,000 + k\u00b7B_p`, with `k = 0.01` FLOP per G_n/s of calibrated cap. The\\\\n+  calibration behind `k` already integrates the 604,800-block dispute window.\\\\n+- The workbook's 19,890 FLOP per H100-eq unit is that formula with H100 SXM peak (989,000) standing\\\\n+  in for calibrated `B_p`.\\\\n+- The runtime (#643, specified in #633 as a settlement-exposure bound) computes\\\\n+  `10,000 + 0.01\u00b7B_p\u00b7604,800\u00b71.25`. It uses D-0418's per-G_n/s coefficient as a per-G_n rate, which\\\\n+  counts the window twice and adds surge: 7,560 FLOP per G_n/s, 756,000\u00d7 the ratified requirement.\\\\n+  An 8\u00d7 H200 host at 40% of peak would need 23.9B FLOP. That is more than the 18.47B FLOP issued by\\\\n+  the end of era 6 (genesis 4.40B, block emission 12.11B, developer subsidy 1.96B), so real-hardware\\\\n+  calibration (#2850) cannot be bonded.\\\\n+\\\\n+The bound was re-derived with today's parameters and the 2026-10 consult's corrections: rewards\\\\n+divide by credited work, rewards are liquid, and settlement exposure is part of the gain. For emission\\\\n+fraud the floor is `k_min = P\u00b7W/(c\u00b7T)`, with `P\u00b7W` = 43.5M FLOP of miner pot per window in era 0,\\\\n+`c` the effective catch probability and `T` the network credited throughput. The gain never exceeds\\\\n+`P\u00b7W`, so the uncapped linear curve over-deters at the top, and D-0418's no-cap invariant stands.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Decision (proposed):**\\\\n+\\\\n+1. **One unit.** The capacity coefficient is FLOP per G_n/s of **calibrated** cap `B_p`. The exposure\\\\n+   window is inside the coefficient (`k` is sized against gain over the window). The requirement\\\\n+   **MUST NOT** multiply by the revocation or dispute window again.\\\\n+2. **Surge is a separate margin.** `\u03c3 = miner_stake_surge_multiplier_ppm / 10\u2076 \u2265 1` multiplies only the\\\\n+   capacity term:\\\\n+   `required_self_stake(B_p) = min_miner_self_stake + \u03c3\u00b7k\u00b7B_p`.\\\\n+   Whether `\u03c3` applies to every cap or only to provisional/SOFT caps stays with E.33. Until then it\\\\n+   applies to every cap, as the runtime does now.\\\\n+3. **The value of `k` is set at activation, not here.** A later owner decision sets `k`, citing\\\\n+   evidence that it satisfies the security envelope (item 4). The candidate to validate first is\\\\n+   `k = 0.25` FLOP per G_n/s (`VFY/4`) with `\u03c3 = 1.25`. At 40% of peak that is: 1\u00d7 RTX 4090 30,625;\\\\n+   1\u00d7 H100 SXM 133,625; 8\u00d7 H200 999,000; 8\u00d7 B200 2,260,000 FLOP. Analytically it deters liquid,\\\\n+   all-fake emission fraud once credited throughput exceeds about 1.9e8 G_n/s at `c = 0.9`\\\\n+   (7.0e8 at `c = 0.25`). That is a sensitivity result, not a demonstrated bound: `c` is unmeasured,\\\\n+   and enforced detection is dispute-only today.\\\\n+4. **Security envelope and activation gates.** The runtime keeps today's requirement until a value of\\\\n+   `k` is shown to satisfy `c_lower \u00b7 s \u00b7 S_available \u2265 G_max` throughout operation, where:\\\\n+   - `c_lower` is a conservative bound on detection, adjudication **and collection**, not a sampling\\\\n+     rate;\\\\n+   - `G_max` is total retained emission **and settlement** gain, including concurrent and unresolved\\\\n+     exposure, with no collateral counted twice;\\\\n+   - the time until fraudulent crediting stops is bounded, and collateral is retained through\\\\n+     dispute resolution;\\\\n+   - enforcement continues after activation: stale measurements, falling credited throughput or failed\\\\n+     detection liveness block new uncovered exposure, including during bootstrap.\\\\n+\\\\n+   The evidence must also include:\\\\n+   - real-inference calibration (#2850), active or activating in the same upgrade;\\\\n+   - aggregate cap enforcement across a miner's concurrent channels;\\\\n+   - measured detection liveness;\\\\n+   - a reproducible adversarial analysis with runtime tests covering bootstrap, low utilization,\\\\n+     coalitions and capacity exits, with uncertainty margins, where leaving the validated envelope\\\\n+     fails closed.\\\\n+\\\\n+   Activation is a separate owner decision, recorded in Appendix H.\\\\n+5. **Alignment, after ratification and activation:**\\\\n+   - runtime: drop `RevocationLatencyBlocks` from `required_self_stake` and set `CapacityStakePerGflop`;\\\\n+   - `params/` (`miner_capacity_stake_per_gflop`, the revocation and surge descriptions), then\\\\n+     `just verify-params`, the simulator mirror and `check_params.py`;\\\\n+   - the miner-worker bond sizing and faucet sponsor sizing, which mirror the runtime formula and\\\\n+     move with it;\\\\n+   - the Lean `stake_covers_settlement_exposure` statement and the Quint miner-staking spec;\\\\n+   - \u00a76.1, Appendices A and C.1, and the workbook (Projection Input \u00a72), which should use calibrated\\\\n+     `B_p` instead of peak spec;\\\\n+   - the published surfaces that quote 7,560 FLOP per G_n/s: the knowledge pages, the intro and\\\\n+     params pages, the onboarding docs and the runbooks.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Rejected:**\\\\n+\\\\n+- *Keep the runtime formula.* Hardware-scale caps cannot be bonded.\\\\n+- *Keep `k = 0.01`.* It deters only above about 4.8e9 G_n/s credited at `c = 0.9`.\\\\n+- *Ratify `k = 0.25` now.* Bondability and conditional thresholds do not establish deterrence while\\\\n+  `c` is unmeasured (2026-10 consult).\\\\n+- *Settlement-exposure sizing (cap \u00d7 window \u00d7 price per G_n).* The model-registry base price\\\\n+  (0.003 FLOP/G_n) is devnet-scale: at that price a week of 8\u00d7 H200 service bills about 5.7B FLOP. It\\\\n+  needs its own recalibration, and settlement exposure is bounded by escrow and aggregate cap\\\\n+  enforcement, not by this bond.\\\\n+- *A cap or sublinear curve.* Unnecessary, since the gain is bounded by `P\u00b7W`, and D-0418 rejects it.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Owner decision requested:**\\\\n+\\\\n+1. Ratify the unit and window placement now (items 1\u20132).\\\\n+2. Adopt `k = 0.25` as the candidate to validate, or name another; 0.05 and 1.0 are tabulated in the\\\\n+   analysis.\\\\n+3. Approve the security envelope and gates (item 4), which fund the adversarial analysis that sets\\\\n+   `k`.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Specification:** \u00a76.1, Appendices A, C.1, E.33, H; `params/flop-protocol-params.yaml`\\\\n+(`miner_capacity_stake_per_gflop`, `miner_stake_revocation_latency_blocks`,\\\\n+`miner_stake_surge_multiplier_ppm`); analysis.\\\\n+\\\\n+---\\\\n+\\\\n+## D-0533 \u2014 Model-registry base price per G_n: a reference set against emission at a reference throughput\\\\n+\\\\n+**Status:** proposal pending ratification (follow-up to #1361 and D-0532). Nothing changes in the\\\\n+runtime, `params/` or published surfaces until the owner ratifies the method and a later decision\\\\n+sets the value at activation.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Context.** `ModelRegistryBasePricePerGFLOP` = 0.003 FLOP per `G_n` was sized for devnet throughput\\\\n+(about 1e3 `G_n/s` network-wide). Its only stated derivation is a simulator input denominated in USD\\\\n+per GFLOP (analysis).\\\\n+\\\\n+Real-inference calibration (#2850) puts caps near 1e5\u20131e7 `G_n/s` per host. At 0.003, one 8\u00d7 H200\\\\n+host at 40% of peak bills about 9,500 FLOP/s. That is 132\u00d7 the whole era-0 miner pot, or 5.74B FLOP\\\\n+per week against 18.47B FLOP issued by the end of era 6.\\\\n+\\\\n+The price does four jobs today:\\\\n+- it is the gateway's de facto bill: gateway escrow is estimated `G_n` \u00d7 epoch price, and a\\\\n+  cooperative settle pays the whole escrow;\\\\n+- it sets the `certificate_settle` floor;\\\\n+- it is every new model's default price;\\\\n+- base/10 floors publisher overrides.\\\\n+\\\\n+The market factor is inert: `Permill::from_percent(200)` saturates at 100%, so the epoch price\\\\n+always equals the model's price.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Decision (proposed):**\\\\n+\\\\n+1. **Method (to ratify).** The base price is a FLOP-denominated reference, not a peg:\\\\n+   `p_ref = \u03c6 \u00b7 P_m(e) / T_ref`. It is the era-`e` miner emission per credited `G_n` at a reference\\\\n+   network throughput `T_ref`, scaled by `\u03c6`, the ratio of gross fees to the miner emission pot.\\\\n+   - No exchange rate enters.\\\\n+   - The emission rate is the design reference D-0532 uses. Channel payouts do not earn it today\\\\n+     (E.44).\\\\n+2. **Benchmark (to validate, not ratified).**\\\\n+   - The inputs are `\u03c6 = 1` and `T_ref` = 500 H100-equivalent units (the workbook's testnet T3 basis)\\\\n+     \u00d7 740,140 `G_n/s` \u00d7 40% = 1.48e8 `G_n/s`.\\\\n+   - That gives 4.86e-7, so the benchmark is **5e-7 FLOP per `G_n`** (`VFY / 2_000_000`,\\\\n+     500,000,000,000 base units).\\\\n+   - `T_ref` is a scenario, not measured throughput. The parity price scales as `1/u` (1.95e-6 at\\\\n+     10% utilization). On a PCIe-equivalent unit instead of the measured SXM unit, it is about\\\\n+     6.4e-7.\\\\n+   - At 5e-7: a 70B-class 1k-token request costs 0.07 FLOP, an 8\u00d7 H200 host-week bills 0.96M FLOP,\\\\n+     and the publisher floor is 5e-8.\\\\n+3. **Bounds on `\u03c6` (analysis, not ratified).** Let `m` be the miner share of a settlement payment:\\\\n+   0.85 under ratified D-0525, 0.99 in today's runtime.\\\\n+   - **Bond.** If D-0532's envelope counts settlement gain at `p_ref`, the bond must cover\\\\n+     `(1 + m\u03c6)\u00b7k_min(T_ref)`. Holding that to 1.0 FLOP per `G_n/s` at `c = 0.9` gives\\\\n+     `\u03c6 \u2264 ~2`.\\\\n+   - **Wash demand.** Fee leakage deters it only at `\u03c6 \u2265 1/(1\u2212m)` (6.7 to 100), and only if credit\\\\n+     checked the price paid, which it does not. The base price makes no claim against wash demand;\\\\n+     that stays with E.49.\\\\n+4. **Activation (a separate owner decision).** The activated value cites:\\\\n+   - measured eligible credited throughput (indexer realized index, settled `G_n`) and #2850 caps;\\\\n+   - the reward and fee split live at activation (E.44 credit, D-0525 `m`);\\\\n+   - migration of existing `avg` and epoch prices, outstanding gateway quotes and open certificate\\\\n+     channels;\\\\n+   - minimum-escrow, existential-deposit and rounding boundaries;\\\\n+   - audit funding at measured claim frequency and cost.\\\\n+\\\\n+   The value is revisited at each halving (`\u03c6` doubles at constant throughput), or when realized\\\\n+   credited throughput leaves `[T_ref/10, 10\u00b7T_ref]`.\\\\n+5. **D-0532 coupling.**\\\\n+   - Settlement exposure stays bounded by escrow and aggregate cap enforcement, as D-0532 states.\\\\n+   - The adversarial analysis that sets D-0532's `k` adds a settlement term: `m \u00d7 (escrow a miner can\\\\n+     collect in W)`. That counts gateway estimates, publisher prices above `p_ref`, and contract\\\\n+     prices. At exactly `p_ref` it equals `m\u00b7\u03c6\u00b7k_min(T_ref)` per `G_n/s` (0.29\u20130.33 at the benchmark,\\\\n+     `c = 0.9`), and it does not fall as throughput grows.\\\\n+   - The base-price change and D-0532 activation ship in the same upgrade or in a fixed order.\\\\n+     Otherwise hardware-scale caps would meet a 0.003 gateway bill.\\\\n+6. **Coupled items (each a separate owner decision):**\\\\n+   - `rate_G` and `channel_base_per_turn` (E.24), today 1e-18 FLOP per `G_n`, with `p_ref` as the\\\\n+     natural reference;\\\\n+   - audit funding (earmark, `audit_fee_per_turn`, claim frequency), which must stay solvent without\\\\n+     lowering `c`;\\\\n+   - the simulator mirror, which becomes a FLOP-denominated input.\\\\n+7. **Alignment, after activation:**\\\\n+   - the runtime constant and `param_consts.rs`;\\\\n+   - `#[pallet::constant]` exposure;\\\\n+   - the market-factor unit fix (or removal of `MaxMarketFactorPercent`);\\\\n+   - promotion into `params/flop-protocol-params.yaml` with a `check_params.py` entry, then\\\\n+     `just verify-params`;\\\\n+   - a reset of every registered model's `avg` and epoch price;\\\\n+   - the docs that quote 0.003.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Rejected:**\\\\n+\\\\n+- *Keep 0.003.* One host bills 132\u00d7 the miner pot, a single 70B-class request exceeds\\\\n+  `agent_per_tx_limit`, and the base/10 floor blocks hardware-scale publisher prices.\\\\n+- *Halve the base with emission.* Pegs fees to the subsidy.\\\\n+- *Size from the bond (`k/(W\u00b7\u03c3)`).* Makes the bond the price oracle.\\\\n+- *Tier multipliers per `G_n`.* `G_n` per token already scales with model size.\\\\n+- *Ratify 5e-7 now.* `T_ref` is a scenario, and both channel reward credit and the D-0525 split are\\\\n+  unimplemented (2026-10 consult).\\\\n+- *Price high enough to deter wash.* Unbondable under D-0532, and ineffective without a price gate on\\\\n+  credit.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Owner decision requested:**\\\\n+\\\\n+1. Ratify the method (item 1).\\\\n+2. Adopt 5e-7 FLOP per `G_n` as the benchmark to validate, or name another `\u03c6`, `T_ref` or\\\\n+   utilization.\\\\n+3. Approve the activation evidence, the D-0532 coupling and the activation order (items 4\u20135).\\\\n+\\\\n+**Specification:** \u00a712.1 R12.1d, Appendices A, E.24, E.44, E.49; `pallets/runtime/zkverify/src/lib.rs`\\\\n+(`ModelRegistryBasePricePerGFLOP`, `ModelRegistryMaxMarketFactorPercent`); `params/system-settings.yaml`;\\\\n+analysis.\\\"},{\\\"sha\\\":\\\"c1318ba15ade249e32569965f0c60c3d1562395b\\\",\\\"filename\\\":\\\"evidence/check-money-path-vectors.py\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"modified\\\",\\\"additions\\\":25,\\\"deletions\\\":0,\\\"changes\\\":25,\\\"blob_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/blob/56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7/evidence%2Fcheck-money-path-vectors.py\\\",\\\"raw_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/raw/56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7/evidence%2Fcheck-money-path-vectors.py\\\",\\\"contents_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/flop-labs/yellowpaper/contents/evidence%2Fcheck-money-path-vectors.py?ref=56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7\\\",\\\"patch\\\":\\\"@@ -30,6 +30,26 @@\\\\n     \\\\\\\"force-dominance\\\\\\\",\\\\n     \\\\\\\"da-loss-no-prefix\\\\\\\",\\\\n     \\\\\\\"da-loss-cosigned-prefix\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"reservation-slot-settle\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"reservation-slot-expire\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"reservation-slot-timeout\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"reservation-slot-fraud\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"reservation-slot-finalize\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"lease-withdraw-unpinned\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"lease-withdraw-pinned\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"lease-withdraw-nonpublisher\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"lease-withdraw-after-top-up\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"lease-withdraw-outstanding-audit\\\\\\\",\\\\n+}\\\\n+\\\\n+RENT_VECTORS = {\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-provider-replacement\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-multiple-replacements\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-failed-block\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-repeat-assignment\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-partial-epochs\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-extension-new-tariff\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"rent-close-partial-service\\\\\\\",\\\\n }\\\\n \\\\n \\\\n@@ -46,8 +66,13 @@ def validate(corpus: dict, schema: dict) -> tuple[int, int]:\\\\n     landed = [vector for vector in vectors if vector[\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"landed\\\\\\\"]\\\\n     if not landed:\\\\n         raise ValueError(\\\\\\\"money-path corpus has no landed vectors\\\\\\\")\\\\n+    rent = {vector[\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\"] for vector in landed if vector[\\\\\\\"adapter\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"paid-storage-arithmetic\\\\\\\"}\\\\n+    if rent != RENT_VECTORS:\\\\n+        raise ValueError(\\\\\\\"money-path corpus must retain all seven D-0524 arithmetic vectors\\\\\\\")\\\\n     for vector in landed:\\\\n         calls = [call[\\\\\\\"call\\\\\\\"] for call in vector[\\\\\\\"extrinsics\\\\\\\"]]\\\\n+        if vector[\\\\\\\"adapter\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"paid-storage-arithmetic\\\\\\\":\\\\n+            continue  # Schema constrains every call; the pallet rent helper checks amounts.\\\\n         if calls not in ([\\\\\\\"force_settle\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"finalize\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\"force_settle\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\"timeout\\\\\\\"]):\\\\n             raise ValueError(f\\\\\\\"unsupported landed call sequence: {vector['id']}\\\\\\\")\\\\n     return len(landed), len(vectors) - len(landed)\\\"},{\\\"sha\\\":\\\"41e74f81852a55fc447ca8f2ecfad7522c30416e\\\",\\\"filename\\\":\\\"evidence/money-path-v1.json\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"modified\\\",\\\"additions\\\":892,\\\"deletions\\\":30,\\\"changes\\\":922,\\\"blob_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/blob/56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7/evidence%2Fmoney-path-v1.json\\\",\\\"raw_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/raw/56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7/evidence%2Fmoney-path-v1.json\\\",\\\"contents_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/flop-labs/yellowpaper/contents/evidence%2Fmoney-path-v1.json?ref=56410c67b11292e707d32ef32e9c4ff9c02e28c7\\\",\\\"patch\\\":\\\"@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\\\\n   \\\\\\\"$schema\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"money-path-v1.schema.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n   \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"flop-money-path-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\n   \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": {\\\\n-    \\\\\\\"yellowpaper_commit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"21e19594bbc3f73ba8d44e01fc872cb5ab37c1ae\\\\\\\",\\\\n+    \\\\\\\"yellowpaper_commit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"b904b8535619a596c7210cfef5dc5af1000fcd0d\\\\\\\",\\\\n     \\\\\\\"yellowpaper_path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"whitepaper/yellowpaper.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n   },\\\\n   \\\\\\\"vectors\\\\\\\": [\\\\n@@ -642,73 +642,555 @@\\\\n     {\\\\n       \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rent-provider-replacement\\\\\\\",\\\\n       \\\\\\\"family\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rent-ceil\\\\\\\",\\\\n-      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\",\\\\n+      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"landed\\\\\\\",\\\\n       \\\\\\\"decision\\\\\\\": {\\\\n-        \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": null,\\\\n+        \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"D-0524\\\\\\\",\\\\n         \\\\\\\"owner\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core/issues/1965\\\\\\\",\\\\n         \\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\": [\\\\n           \\\\\\\"R5.4e\\\\\\\",\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"R5.4f\\\\\\\"\\\\n+          \\\\\\\"R5.4f\\\\\\\",\\\\n+          \\\\\\\"R5.4n\\\\\\\"\\\\n         ]\\\\n       },\\\\n       \\\\\\\"source_issue\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/yellowpaper/issues/80\\\\\\\",\\\\n-      \\\\\\\"adapter\\\\\\\": null,\\\\n+      \\\\\\\"adapter\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"paid-storage-arithmetic\\\\\\\",\\\\n       \\\\\\\"input\\\\\\\": {\\\\n         \\\\\\\"balances\\\\\\\": {\\\\n           \\\\\\\"reservation_escrow\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\n+          \\\\\\\"payer_refund\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\",\\\\n           \\\\\\\"provider_a\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\",\\\\n           \\\\\\\"provider_b\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"\\\\n         },\\\\n         \\\\\\\"storage\\\\\\\": {\\\\n           \\\\\\\"reserved_bytes\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"term_blocks\\\\\\\": 2,\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"rent_num\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"rent_den\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\",\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"funded_rent\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\n-          \\\\\\\"assignments\\\\\\\": [\\\\n+          \\\\\\\"tranches\\\\\\\": [\\\